"""
ABACUS v0.5.0 - build hook.  Writes abacus_pkg.vhd next to this file.  Pure python (the builder runs it
with the system interpreter).

The look is measured from the photo (WIN_20230605_01_03_50): rows of glossy red beads between blue/green
bands, mirrored about the bead rows (period 495 lines), one bead every 188 px, the beads changing
character across the frame (dark maroon with green lenses and 'eyes' on the left, bright red ovals in
the middle, pink-cored hourglass beads on the right).

  field       ONE scalar field s(x, d) drives the colourizer.  It is a measured knot grid:
              32 rows (d = 0 .. 248 lines from the bead-row centre, every 8 lines) x 128 columns
              (x = 0 .. 1905 virtual px, every 15 px), bilinear between knots.  Fitted to the photo by
              alternating a per-pixel field solve, a least-squares knot fit and a palette re-learn
              (.heirloom_work/rb_abacus/kalt8.py).
  colourizer  a 1-D palette over s (512 entries): bright red -> dark red -> maroon -> pink/cream glint ->
              olive -> dark green -> navy -> red band-edge line -> violet -> green -> teal -> blue.

Package contents:
  C_AB_KNOT   4096 x 8   knot ROM, address = row * 128 + column, s in 1/255.
  C_AB_PAL    512 x 32   palette ROM {Y (10, luma pre-scaled 16/13), U = Cr (10), V = Cb (10), 00} in the
                         hardware convention (U register = Cr, V = Cb), Y clamped at 940.
  C_AB_GL     256 x 64   gloss ROM.  The photo's specular glints (cream / white arcs on the bead tops and
                         bottoms, orange and yellow sparks, grey band-edge glints) and the left third's
                         lenses and eyes (green, navy, amber) are thin runs measured column by column from
                         one tile copy of the photo (gcol4.py): 257 columns every 8 horizontal units
                         (7.5 virtual px), 2 slots each.  Word c holds columns c and c + 1; each 16-bit slot
                         entry is {D centre in 2-line steps (7), J jump to the next column (1), W half-width
                         class (3), A amplitude (2), C colour class (3)}; slot k of column c sits in bits
                         16k+15..16k, of column c + 1 in 16(k+2)+15..16(k+2).
  f_ab_gc     the 8 gloss colour classes {Y, U, V} (same convention as the palette), as a case (logic).
"""
